# =============================================================================
# OPERATION ANKAA — environment
# Copy to `.env.local` for development, and set the same values on the host
# (Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for production.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SITE'S OWN ADDRESS — REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH.
#
# Feeds `metadataBase`, every canonical URL, the OG/Twitter card URL,
# sitemap.xml, robots.txt and the JSON-LD `@id`. `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is required:
# the value is inlined at build time and read during static generation.
#
# Without it the build prints a warning and falls back to `https://ankaa.example`
# — an RFC 2606 reserved domain that can never be registered, chosen precisely
# so a misconfigured deploy is obviously broken rather than quietly pointing at
# somebody else's website. Do not "fix" it by inventing a plausible domain.
#
# Origin only. No trailing slash.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://ankaa.example

# =============================================================================
# THE ENQUIRY FORM'S TRANSPORT — WIRED UP 2026-08-22 (Resend).
#
# `deliverEnquiry()` in src/lib/enquiry-transport.ts is implemented. The form
# now really sends, which means `sent` is a reachable state and the copy the
# visitor reads — «وصل طلبك إلى الجمعية.» — is a promise about the real world.
# Read the header of that file before touching anything here.
#
# THE KEY GOES IN `.env.local`, NOT IN THIS FILE.
# `.gitignore` line 34 is `.env*`, so `.env.local` is never committed — this
# example file is tracked precisely so nobody has to guess the variable names.
# Copy it once:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local        (PowerShell: copy .env.example .env.local)
#
# then paste the real key into `.env.local` and restart the dev server. Set the
# same variables on the host for production (Vercel: Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for the form to send at all. Without it `deliverEnquiry()` returns
# `not-configured` and the visitor is told, honestly, that nothing was sent —
# which is the same behaviour the site had before the transport existed.
#
# Get one at resend.com → API Keys. Starts `re_`.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHO THE EMAIL COMES FROM. Optional — defaults to Resend's shared sandbox
# sender, `onboarding@resend.dev`.
#
# ⚠️ THE SANDBOX SENDER CAN ONLY DELIVER TO THE ADDRESS THAT OWNS THE API KEY.
# That is Resend's rule. It is perfect for proving the pipeline works and it
# CANNOT be used to reach the association.
#
# TO GO LIVE, both of these change together:
#   1. verify the association's domain in Resend (it prints SPF/DKIM records;
#      paste them into the domain's DNS — Cloudflare, if that is the registrar)
#   2. set this to an address on that verified domain, e.g. no-reply@<domain>
#      AND set `contactDelivery.value` in src/content/placeholders.ts to the
#      association's monitored inbox
# Change one without the other and every send is refused with a 403.
#
# Receiving is a separate job from sending: Cloudflare Email Routing (free)
# forwards info@<domain> to a real mailbox, but it CANNOT send. That is why a
# provider is needed here as well.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENQUIRY_FROM=onboarding@resend.dev

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used. Kept as a note: if the association ever mandates its own mail
# server instead of a provider, `deliverEnquiry()` is the only function that
# changes, and these are the variables it would read.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
